.TH ISA-CHECK 8 "November 2026" "isa-check 0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
isa-check \- list or probe processor architecture variants
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B isa-check
.RI [ --table " PATH" ]
.RI [ VARIANT ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B isa-check
reads dpkg's variant table and checks the CPU flags of every processor reported
in
.IR /proc/cpuinfo .
When invoked without a variant, it prints every compatible variant for the
current architecture, one per line, in table order from highest to lowest.
.PP
When a variant is specified, no output is produced on success. An unsupported
variant produces a diagnostic listing its missing features.
.PP
The proc filesystem must already be mounted at
.IR /proc .
.B isa-check
does not mount it. If cpuinfo cannot be opened or read, the command reports an
error and exits with status 2.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --table " PATH"
Read the variant table from
.I PATH
instead of
.IR /usr/share/dpkg/varianttable .
.TP
.B --help
Print usage information.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested variant is supported, or at least one compatible variant was
listed.
.TP
.B 1
The requested variant is unsupported, or no compatible variants were found.
.TP
.B 2
A usage, variant table, or cpuinfo error occurred.
.SH EXAMPLES
List compatible variants:
.PP
.nf
.RS
$ isa-check
amd64v3
amd64v2
amd64v1
.RE
.fi
.PP
Probe for amd64v3 in an installer script:
.PP
.nf
.RS
if isa-check amd64v3; then
    variant=amd64v3
fi
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/dpkg/varianttable
.br
.I /proc/cpuinfo
